  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Loop Lab CE Incubator programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Loop Lab CE Incubator project aims to support start-ups in Nigeria (focus Lagos) that offer CE-oriented products and services that can be delivered to corporate clients. Start-ups who take part in the programme do so in partnership with an existing or potential client. The start-ups  get the opportunity to collaborate and work with like-minded individuals to start building and scaling up their businesses. The incubation program offers five types of training and support to new ventures: peer networking &amp; mentorship, business advisory services, taught programming, prototype development, and demonstration days to showcase products and services to clients and investors.The ultimate goal of this project is to strengthen the Nigerian CE start-up ecosystem, improve the success rates of new partnerships (including with Dutch businesses), and combat youth unemployment.</narrative>
  </description>
